bri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Hexokinase IV Is Regulated by Sequestration (and Transcription)</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="285" name="Google Shape;285;p39"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="1371600"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="A diagram illustrating the regulation of hexokinase IV (glucokinase) by sequestration in the nucleus.&#xA;The diagram begins on the left with a long pink box representing a capillary, with glucose inside the box. An arrow from glucose points through a GLUT2 image breaking through the plasma membrane. This arrow points to glucose in cytosol. From glucose is an arrow pointing down to glucose 6-phosphate, which has an arrow pointing down to fructose 6-phosphate. Glucose also has a dashed arrow pointing right then down to a green triangle in a circle. The fructose 6-phosphate has a dashed arrow pointing right, then up to a triangle in a circle. Between the two triangles in a circle are reversible arrows pointing from hexokinase IV in a blue oval in cytosol to hexokinase IV in a blue oval in the nucleus. Below the hexokinase IV oval is a green oval representing regulatory pattern. " id="286" name="Google Shape;286;p39"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="304800" y="1679575"/><a:ext cx="8534400" cy="4187825"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rec